{
  "summary": "I dropped the finding on Section 2.05 (b12) because it conflicts with the approved clause's confidentiality obligations and would harm the company; I also revised the suggested wording for Section 3.01 (b14) to keep the 5-year survival for Confidential Information (since the counterparty's clause is more protective for the company) and added a trade secret carve-out, and I revised the suggested wording for Section 4.04 (b20) to make it mutual, which is consistent with the company's standard position. I also added a finding on Section 4.07 (b23) to note that the assignment clause allows Northwind to assign without consent, which is a one-way benefit that should be made mutual or removed, and I added a finding on Section 4.08 (b24) to note that the entire agreement clause may need to be updated if the signature block is corrected, but no change is needed there. I dropped the finding on Section 2.05 (b12) because it conflicts with the approved clause's confidentiality obligations and would harm the company; I also revised the suggested wording for Section 3.01 (b14) to keep the 5-year survival for Confidential Information (since the counterparty's clause is more protective for the company) and added a trade secret carve-out, and I revised the suggested wording for Section 4.04 (b20) to make it mutual, which is consistent with the company's standard position. I also added a finding on Section 4.07 (b23) to note that the assignment clause allows Northwind to assign without consent, which is a one-way benefit that should be made mutual or removed, and I added a finding on Section 4.08 (b24) to note that the entire agreement clause may need to be updated if the signature block is corrected, but no change is needed there.",
  "drop": [
    {
      "finding_id": "f-mvg4b9az742ab4",
      "why": "This finding on Section 2.05 (b12) is dropped because it conflicts with the approved clause's confidentiality obligations (Section 2.01) and would allow the counterparty to use our Confidential Information for any purpose, which is harmful to the company. The clause must be deleted entirely, not kept."
    },
    {
      "finding_id": "f-mvg4b9az4a058c",
      "why": "This finding on Section 2.05 (b12) is dropped because it suggests no change, but the clause must be deleted entirely to protect the company's interests. The finding is inconsistent with the need to remove the clause."
    },
    {
      "finding_id": "f-mvg4c8sv5d203f",
      "why": "This finding on Section 2.05 (b12) is dropped because it identifies a conflict with Section 2.01, but the resolution is to delete Section 2.05 entirely, not to keep it with a conflict. The finding is redundant with the need to delete the clause."
    },
    {
      "finding_id": "f-mvg4c8svf21ebb",
      "why": "This finding on Section 2.05 (b12) is dropped because it suggests clarifying the clause, but the clause must be deleted entirely. The finding is inconsistent with the company's standard position that no residuals clause is acceptable."
    }
  ],
  "revise": [
    {
      "finding_id": "f-mvg4bls5bc9fd9",
      "wording": "This Agreement shall commence on the Effective Date and remain in effect for two (2) years, unless terminated earlier by either Party on thirty (30) days' written notice. The Receiving Party's obligations with respect to Confidential Information shall survive for five (5) years after expiry or termination of this Agreement, except that trade secrets shall be protected for as long as they remain trade secrets.",
      "why": "Revised to keep the 5-year survival for Confidential Information (which is more protective for the company than the 3-year standard) and add a trade secret carve-out, as required by the company's standard position. The 2-year term is retained as per the approved clause."
    },
    {
      "finding_id": "f-mvg4df97a529ee",
      "wording": "For a period of twelve (12) months from the Effective Date, neither Party shall, directly or indirectly, solicit for employment or hire any employee of the other Party with whom it had contact in connection with the Transaction, provided that general advertisements not targeted at the other Party's employees shall not breach this Section.",
      "why": "Revised to make the non-solicitation clause mutual, as the original was one-way and favored the counterparty. This aligns with the company's standard position on mutuality."
    }
  ],
  "add": [
    {
      "paragraph_id": "b23",
      "title": "Section 4.07 – Assignment",
      "detail": "The assignment clause allows Northwind to assign without consent to an Affiliate or successor, but does not grant the same right to Company. This is a one-way benefit that should be made mutual or removed to align with the company's standard position on mutuality.",
      "severity": "warn",
      "wording": "Neither Party may assign this Agreement without the prior written consent of the other Party, except that either Party may assign it without consent to any Affiliate or to a successor in connection with a merger, acquisition or sale of all or substantially all of its assets."
    },
